  "notes": "Nonprofit organization (not a government); treated as entirely business-type, GAAP. Receipts: 'Grants and contributions' 865,715 is public support; reported receipts total = Total public support and revenues 1,894,055 (p2; revenues alone 1,028,340). Zero-valued lines (credit loss recovery, gain on disposal, zero program lines) omitted. Disbursements are Program services and General and administration (Total expenses 1,882,552). Net assets 6,757,546 + 1,894,055 - 1,882,552 = 6,769,049. Functional expenses detail uses the Total column (program services + G&A combined) for 2025; the function category is economic development for all, so G&A portion (70,982) is not separated by line in detail; Bank service charges, dues, insurance, professional services etc. are mostly G&A. Prior-year (2024) columns ignored. Balance sheet is the Statements of Financial Position (nonprofit, no deferred items). Cash flow statement is indirect method; operating and investing nets recorded, no financing section. Trimmed pages: 1 financial position, 2 activities 2025, 3 activities 2024, 4 functional expenses 2025, 5 functional expenses 2024, 6 cash flows. Read pages 1-6 of 6",
